> Things don't necessary merge on floor as they are generated, but
> picking up merges if paid or unpaid and known or unkown BUC and
> enchantment. So if we restrict the enchantment to 0 or +1 (-1 for
> cursed) you might have: 
> 
> a - a dagger
> b - a dagger (unpaid, 3 zorkmids)
> c - a dagger
> d - a dagger (unpaid, 3 zorkmids)
> e - a dagger
> f - a dagger (unpaid, 3 zorkmids)
> g - a dagger
> h - a dagger (unpaid, 6 zorkmids)
> i - a dagger
> j - a dagger (unpaid, 6 zorkmids)
> k - a dagger
> l - a dagger (unpaid, 6 zorkmids)
> m - an uncursed dagger
> n - an uncursed dagger (unpaid, 3 zorkmids)
> o - a cursed dagger
> p - a cursed dagger (unpaid, 3 zorkmids)
> q - a blessed dagger
> r - a blessed dagger (unpaid, 3 zorkmids)
> s - an uncursed dagger
> t - an uncursed dagger (unpaid, 6 zorkmids)
> u - a cursed dagger
> v - a cursed dagger (unpaid, 6 zorkmids)
> w - a blessed dagger
> x - a blessed dagger (unpaid, 6 zorkmids)
> y - a +0 dagger
> z - a +0 dagger (unpaid, 3 zorkmids)
> A - a cursed +0 dagger
> B - a cursed +0 dagger (unpaid, 3 zorkmids)
> C - a blessed +0 dagger
> D - a blessed +0 dagger (unpaid, 3 zorkmids)
> E - a +1 dagger
> F - a +1 dagger (unpaid, 6 zorkmids)
> G - a cursed -1 dagger
> H - a cursed -1 dagger (unpaid, 6 zorkmids)
> I - a blessed +1 dagger
> J - a blessed +1 dagger (unpaid, 6 zorkmids)
> 
> That's 36 inventory slots. If count out the unpaid daggers then it's
> 18 inventory slots, but if we the introduce -2 cursed and +2 blessed
> or uncursed daggers in the picture we increase it to 27.
> 
> Now if you drop these on altar and look at them you have the same 27 
> 'stacks' but if you pick them up the former totally unknown will merge
> with the BUC known and you get only 18 stacks.
> 
> This might confuse almost anybody but it is not a bug in NetHack.
